{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron","id":469923,"title":"God in the Iron","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-06T00:13:41-07:00","id":469923,"title":"God in the Iron","content":"A thought occured to me. A simple connection between the fae and the God Machine could be had by making that famous broken pact between Gentry and Iron in some connected to the Machine...in other words, the essence of Iron is the God-Machine or in some other way tied directly to it. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T00:35:54-07:00","id":469948,"title":"","content":"Given the way Contracts are shown to be made and the implications about how those interactions mixed in with God's tendency to not deal but rather just subjugate all other gods?<br /> <br /> No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:52:17-07:00","id":470249,"title":"","content":"Well what if the god of iron is subjugated by the machine? It could have been one of the few the machine resonated enough with to embrace or enslave without error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T18:31:28-07:00","id":470566,"title":"","content":"It's not like the Fae deal with spirits or gods. They deal with the thing itself. You aren't talking to a spirit of the hearth or the supernal god of hearths when you sign a Contract, you are literally talking to all Hearths via the Wyrd, and you are interacting with it in a way no one else understands.<br /> <br /> If anything, the Machine is subjugated by <i>iron</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T20:28:20-07:00","id":470723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron?p=470566#post470566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like the Fae deal with spirits or gods. They deal with the thing itself. You aren't talking to a spirit of the hearth or the supernal god of hearths when you sign a Contract, you are literally talking to all Hearths via the Wyrd, and you are interacting with it in a way no one else understands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've often found it amusing that the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GlassCannon\" target=\"_blank\">contemporary nickname</a> for an exceedingly fragile implement of devastation sounds like the sort of fanciful widget that'd be right at home in Faerie, particularly considering that the ephemerality of fae power tends to manifest like trump cards in certain games (where a given card can be used to beat any other but is itself beaten by even the lowest available card).<br /> <br /> Yes, the fae's power can often be banished as easily as a stray thought. It doesn't change the fact that it is <i>going</i> to blow through in the first place because Story Is King, or that permanence is immaterial to a well-played hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T22:27:27-07:00","id":470922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron?p=469948#post469948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the way Contracts are shown to be made and the implications about how those interactions mixed in with God's tendency to not deal but rather just subjugate all other gods?<br /> <br /> No.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blame it on the combination of my paralegal training and playing too much Phoenix Wright, but....OBJECTION! Could you please explain in more detail what precisely has been shown about the way Contracts are made, bearing in mind how subjective these things can be? Also, later on you say that 'If anything, Iron subjugates the Machine'. I think I'm missing your point. Whether the Machine is beholden to Iron or Iron is beholden to the Machine or even if the one is merely one aspect or mask of the other, doesn't it all lead to the same result? Whether passively or directly, the God Machine becomes an enemy of the True Fae due to whatever connection it possesses with Iron...and perhaps the broader fact that the Gentry represent too chaotic a force to be ignored...or that the Fae are rivals trying to impose their own mad order upon Arcadia/dreams/Earth just as the God Machine wishes to. <br /> <br /> What I find interesting is that there are many legends of fairies being driven away or even killed by prayer, church bells, and angels. In certain parts of the globe a Christian priest was called upon to cleanse a house of the Fae much like they would demonic presences. In addition to making these stories allergens of various gentry, we have here an alternative explanation- the God Machine is waging occasional war upon Arcadia and by extension its refugees known as the Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T22:41:23-07:00","id":470930,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7876756\" target=\"_blank\">Well, if we want to play that game....</a><br /> <br /> Spoilers contain the relevant text without the fun, for those who might not have it work or want to quote it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A clear and thorough reading of Rites of Spring Chapter 3 reveals the explanation of Contracts being made with the thing itself, building on the humanization of the world motifs found in faerie tales as mentioned in my Demon/Changeling essay. <br /> <br /> The line about iron subjugating the Machine is a throwaway line.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine's subjugation of all of reality under it's idea of order is reason enough for the Gentry, who thrive in the changing nature of their Legends, to be marked as an enemy. There is no need to supernaturally make it worse, as well as narratively weaker and less interesting, by making the God-Machine be the representative of Iron, at least from a canon perspective.<br /> <br /> As Always, what happens at your own table is your own business.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T23:26:15-07:00","id":470973,"title":"","content":"I also want to stipulate that I'm not saying the Strangers and God aren't at each others throats. Of course they are. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/253106-apocalypse-vault?p=255358#post255358\">I even wrote a piece based on that.</a><br /> <br /> I just don't see a reason to bring Iron in on it. The metal bones of God are the least interesting part of its' being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-07-2015, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T22:47:45-07:00","id":494423,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the original idea in my head was less about them being connected directly and more about some poor mad group of changeling Bridge-Burners desperate to find a weapon against the Fae that start making more and more desperate attempts to contact Iron the way they can contact other Contract related forces to try. You know, beg to be forgiven from whatever offense the Gentry committed and asking to be empowered as the servants of the one thing in existence the Gentry fear.<br /> <br /> And one night, they get an answer. <br /> <br /> It just later occurred to me later that the thing claiming to be Iron doesn't even have to be lying. So I figured I'd share that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T01:00:22-07:00","id":494503,"title":"","content":"I'd think the God-Machine does reach into at least the Hedge using Crash the Gates... Demons can enter the Hedge after all and if they are looking for a place to call Hell, why isn't every Demon just making their way there?<br /> Yes, it's different than Arcadia, though True Fae walk the Hedge just as much as changelings and hobs and I firmly believe the G-M has some connect into the Hedge, more through it's occult side than it's technological side of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> But now I have need to write of a changeling who dug into a certain spot of the brambles to make a Hollow and unearthed an area of blood-greased cogs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T04:28:38-07:00","id":494589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron?p=494503#post494503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think the God-Machine does reach into at least the Hedge using Crash the Gates... Demons can enter the Hedge after all and if they are looking for a place to call Hell, why isn't every Demon just making their way there?<br /> Yes, it's different than Arcadia, though True Fae walk the Hedge just as much as changelings and hobs and I firmly believe the G-M has some connect into the Hedge, more through it's occult side than it's technological side of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, realistically they can never leave without help. The Hedge is a horrifying and torturous place to even those who have an affinity for it, knowingly leaving one form of bondage to freely enter another, completely alien and unfathomable one is likely be to unattractive to most Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:19:07-07:00","id":494846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron?p=494589#post494589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because, realistically they can never leave without help. The Hedge is a horrifying and torturous place to even those who have an affinity for it, knowingly leaving one form of bondage to freely enter another, completely alien and unfathomable one is likely be to unattractive to most Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides which, that Aether you can still recover Hedgeside comes from <i>somewhere</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:34:38-07:00","id":495131,"title":"","content":"So the God-Machine reaches into the Hedge at least, due to where Aether comes from.<br /> <br /> Arcadia of course is still up in there if it's in reach of the God-Machine or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:40:42-07:00","id":495321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron?p=495131#post495131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the God-Machine reaches into the Hedge at least, due to where Aether comes from.<br /> <br /> Arcadia of course is still up in there if it's in reach of the God-Machine or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Arcadia is worse than anything the GM can throw at you. Demons don't have the <i>reality</i> that humans do, and the way their Cover works means that the narrative nature of Arcadia would pretty much chain them down just as surely as the God-Machine would.<br /> <br /> Sure, the God Machine isn't there... but what's there isn't much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T07:37:13-07:00","id":497437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/469923-god-in-the-iron?p=494589#post494589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, realistically they can never leave without help. The Hedge is a horrifying and torturous place to even those who have an affinity for it, knowingly leaving one form of bondage to freely enter another, completely alien and unfathomable one is likely be to unattractive to most Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe? I think this statement has a lot of assumptions about the how the Hedge and the GM interact. We know that the God Machine likely has gears in the Hedge that aren't being torn apart, so modifying those wouldn't be too bad.<br /> <br /> That said, there's a very good reason why they're not moving en masse into the Hedge. Only one of four Agendas (Tempters/Builders) thinks that Hell is a physical place. The others either want to escape it, focus on destroying the God Machine, or reach some form of demonic enlightenment. In the Tempter Agenda, there's a good portion of them that appreciate the creature comforts of reality, or are in love with humans, or want to keep their cultists, not run away from them - stuff that generally won't work out in the Hedge. These guys want Hell on Earth.<br /> <br /> So, the majority of demons aren't moving into the Hedge (or Hisil, Astral, Underworld, Inferno, etc) for the simple reason of it not fitting the vast majority of what they want out of Hell. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of Arcadia versus the God Machine. There's actually some pretty strong thematic connections between the God Machine and Wyrd, most of which revolve around them both being opposites. The fae are whimsical, transformative, pretty chaotic when all is said and done. In many ways, its art personified. It is Lady Luck smiling and mocking you, twisting things as suit her fancy. The God Machine is Order. It has plans. It is the inevitable march of Fate going towards its inevitable conclusion with mathematical precision, heavily grounded in reality. Meanwhile, all the stories about Iron all contain different things. The most popular seems to be Iron as a sentient being pissed at the Fae for broken a contract. One was about making a deal with humans against all the things in the night. The third was &quot;Foe of All Unreason,&quot; which iron is the embodiment of science-driven development instead of imagination, which fits with the whole God Machine.<br /> <br /> Now, given that the &quot;aspects of reality&quot; that changelings make Contracts with are very ill defined (I can argue that spirits and astral reflections are, by definition, aspects of reality), I see no reason why we can't say that the God Machine is somehow tied to Iron in 1e. In 2e? There's a shift towards being more Narrative driven, and powers changing depending on what your Seeming is (more like werewolf gifts?) so I don't want to talk about that without more information on 2e Lost. Even then, all the comparisons pale before the idea for a good story.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, in this light, I don't see why there can't be a connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}